#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0309 expect=violation domain=APMH
#note "Positive control on the rule's intended AP-- population: DOMAIN is present but 2 characters, not 4, so has_not_equal_length 4 fires. Together with the -valid- twin this proves the rule executes and discriminates on APMH, which is what makes the -absent-DOMAIN-SUPPLB scenario a statement about SCOPE rather than about the fold."
#expectViolationCount 1
dataset APMH label="Associated Persons Medical History"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col APID     type=Char label="Associated Persons Identifier"
col MHSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col MHTERM   type=Char label="Reported Term for the Medical History"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | MH | AP-701-1015 | 1 | ASTHMA
CDISCPILOT01 | MH | AP-701-1023 | 2 | ECZEMA
---
